    "body": "Hmm, I know it is an old issue, but the sentence doesn't make much sense. Click events aren't queued. Same with dblclick. Those are dispatched based on down/up events. And the task which dispatches up dispatches a trusted click event. (but of course up event listener could dispatch an untrusted click too, and that shouldn't get special treatment). I think this text should talk about trusted events.",
